WEBVTT

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:02.750
Lord Villar...

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:06.500
I'd like you to assist Starck
in our battle against Waldlind.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:09.760
Lord Pavel...

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:13.390
The Union is currently
in peace talks with the Alliance.

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:15.800
I'm not holding my breath
for the Union to act!

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.140
All we need is for you to make a move!

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:22.350
Once you do, Ozeri and Bultava
will surely secede from the Alliance!

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:25.270
If you do make a move, Lord Villar,

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:28.900
I will convince my father
to send troops from Dartania.

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.820
In my opinion, Lord Milza is absolutely right.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:37.080
For Altirk to survive, even if it means
breaking off from the Union,

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.160
we should fight.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:45.080
I'll be a laughingstock for leaving the Union
for not getting my way at the Lords' Congress.

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:49.300
Not only that, but I don't wish
to break Lord Alexis's heart.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:53.300
But it's Lord Alexis himself
who's trying to destroy us!

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.930
Please, rather than uphold your honor,
choose the path that allows Altirk to survive!

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.180
Siluca! Refrain yourself!

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.390
I cannot bring myself to betray Lord Alexis.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.690
It appears I don't need your opinion.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.860
Return to your domain with Theo.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:14.950
Understood.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:19.410
Theo.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:22.830
I'm counting on you.

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:28.250
I understand, sir.

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:35.970
What that mage said seemed
like sound advice to me.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:40.180
It's my call to make, not yours.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:43.770
I suggest you show some restraint, as well.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:47.400
You should pledge fealty to Lady Marrine
immediately, and agree to be subjugated.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:51.860
That's up to me to decide, not you!

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:54.860
I have no intention of
allying with Marrine Kreische!

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:02.740
I'll be keeping an eye
on Lord Pavel's battle till the end.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:08.040
I'm interested to see how Waldlind will
assault the perilous Isthmus of Penelope.

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:46.260
It wasn't like you to act like that.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:50.190
I couldn't see any other way to save Altirk.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:56.150
It's unlikely to avoid a war against the Alliance,
so it's a matter of how we prepare, right?

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:59.360
It will be hard to change the tides of war,

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.200
so our only hope is to muster
as many troops as possible.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:08.330
Right!

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:10.410
Starting tomorrow,
I'll be touring the domain.

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.670
And you'll be joining me, this time.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:34.690
Seems like they're not ready to accept us yet.

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:36.860
There's nothing we can do.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:41.190
After all, there must be
a lot of Dimitrie's kin here.

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:42.400
That's right.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:50.200
I plan on heading near the Bultava border.
Let's move on to the next village.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:52.080
Right.

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:50.850
Let's take shelter over there.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:02.030
What a sorry sight we are!

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:05.200
It won't be good if we're in these wet clothes.

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:06.990
We need to get changed, right?

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:23.210
No good. The firewood's damp.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.680
Are you cold?

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:30.550
Yes. A little.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:32.010
Then...

00:06:33.770 --> 00:06:34.890
Let's do this.

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:38.350
You're not cold now, are you?

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:40.060
N-No...

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:06.210
Sitting here like this reminds me of
how I used to camp out in the rain.

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:11.510
That's right, you used to
wander all over the place.

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:12.470
Yeah.

00:07:12.470 --> 00:07:15.180
Traveling alone really made me feel lonely.

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:20.810
I'm glad to have you by my side, Sir Theo.

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:25.070
This isn't the outcome I had in mind,

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:30.320
but you've been so swamped lately,
I wanted to give you a break.

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:34.370
After the Lords' Congress and
that thing with Lord Villar,

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:36.410
I thought it'd be a nice change of scenery.

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:38.080
Is that why you brought me?

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:44.340
Also, since you've been going to Castle Unicorn
so much, I guess I was kind of worried.

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:47.960
That you'd end up becoming Villar's vassal...

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:49.340
That'd never happen.

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:52.590
You went so far as to give up
your court rank to preserve our contract.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:57.270
As long as you need me,
I intend to serve you forever!

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:00.980
Looks like I haven't gotten through to you.

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:03.100
What do you mean?

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:12.990
You've always been thoughtful,
and risked your life for me.

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:18.500
So I've always wanted to live up to that,
and tried to protect you.

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:22.960
When Lord Villar tried to
take you away from me,

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:25.500
I didn't think twice
about giving up my court rank.

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:29.260
You also rescued me
from the Black Witch's spell.

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:31.680
Of course I'd rescue you!

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:34.390
Because you're someone important to me.

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:39.270
That's what I wanted you to know.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:42.310
R-Right.

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:47.190
U-Um...

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:51.950
Are you aware of my feelings for you?

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:55.280
Well, I did have a feeling...

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:59.290
But I thought it might just be
me imagining things.

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:02.790
Um!

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:05.790
This is an extremely important issue,
so I want to make it clear.

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:12.550
Sir Theo, can I take it
that you're in love with me?

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:14.760
You're really gonna make me go there?

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:17.800
You really are a mage, aren't you?

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:29.900
Of course...
I'm in love with you.

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:04.730
Fire!

00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:17.450
N-No way!

00:10:38.890 --> 00:10:40.890
Who is that Shadow-like knight?

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:42.970
Most likely, that's Milza Kuches.

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:46.180
So that's the Black Prince of Dartania.

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:01.370
If we're going to attack the Starck fortress,

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:04.370
our only option is to advance along
a narrow one-way path along the shore.

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:07.790
However, these rocky hills tower over
the path on its eastern side,

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:12.130
while there are ten ships with catapults
moored in the sea to the west.

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:18.010
According to my sources, a Dartanian fleet is
providing Lord Pavel with food and supplies,

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:20.180
and are moored in nearby waters.

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:23.810
It would be impossible
to reach the peninsula by ship.

00:11:23.810 --> 00:11:26.890
Even if we managed to get there,
it won't be easy to defeat Milza.

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:31.150
What if we climbed the hills,
and attacked the fortress from the ridge?

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:33.820
But if we climb those hills,

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:36.150
we'll be forced to leave
our horses and armor behind.

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:40.030
I do have one idea.

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:43.120
In this wetland known as the Rotten Sea,

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:46.660
a form of Chaos Hazard
called miasma appears frequently.

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:51.420
This miasma can also be
generated artificially, I believe.

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:54.170
So you're going to generate
miasma, and then what?

00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:58.670
Let the wind carry it
into the Isthmus of Penelope.

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:07.100
The soldiers will be forced to either
forfeit the castle or succumb to the miasma.

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:11.440
Then, if we time our attack
for when the miasma clears,

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:15.190
even the strongest of fortresses
will be sure to fall in an instant.

00:12:15.190 --> 00:12:19.070
Using Chaos Hazard is a violation
of the Lords' Code!

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:22.110
If we don't fight fair and square,
even if we were to win–

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:23.200
It's a good strategy.

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:25.160
- What?
- Lady Marrine!

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:30.370
Won't Waldlind come under fire
for using dirty tactics to win?

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:33.710
I have no intention of becoming
a virtuous but inept leader.

00:12:35.340 --> 00:12:39.960
Even if I should incur infamy far and wide,
I intend to hold sway over the continent!

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:46.220
If you're prepared, then we will obey
your command and fight.

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:49.600
Then, I command you!

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:52.850
Viscount Pavel Murado,
and the Lords and soldiers allied to him,

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:55.310
will not be allowed to surrender.

00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:59.320
Half-baked benevolence will
be seen as weakness on our part.

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:02.490
Show the world what becomes
of those who defy Waldlind,

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:08.870
and force the indecisive Lords of Bultava and Ozeri
to choose either subjugation or death!

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:10.450
As you wish!

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:18.840
I have a favor to ask of you.

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:19.710
What is it?

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:23.720
I want you to contact Milza,
the Prince of Dartania.

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:35.650
It's almost time for
the wind to change direction...

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:42.150
Now, then, let's begin.

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:45.530
A lake bed is a silent thing.

00:13:45.530 --> 00:13:48.530
Yet, at times, it becomes a vacillating swell.

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:50.870
Swirl!

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:02.210
Red poison, sweet poison,

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:05.760
The poison stagnating in the mud
consume each other.

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:09.640
Poison becomes foam, fog, then haze,
and is carried by the wind.

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:11.470
Rise up!

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:26.650
Are you all right?

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:30.530
I just learned firsthand
how overpowering miasma can be.

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:35.040
Meaning there's no question that
the fortress soldiers will be incapacitated.

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:44.550
Miasma!
Miasma's coming this way!

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:54.390
Cover your mouths with cloths!
Hang in there until the miasma's gone!

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:56.600
The wind will change direction eventually!

00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:59.600
If only we had Lord Milza's help...

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:01.540
How unfortunate for you.

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:05.050
Is this...

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:10.130
...how the continent's
most powerful knights fight?

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:15.010
It is the Kreische clan's style
to fight rationally, that is all.

00:16:20.690 --> 00:16:22.270
Viscount Pavel Murado.

00:16:23.270 --> 00:16:25.480
I receive thy Crest as my own.

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:47.460
Not what I was expecting,
but entertaining.

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:50.420
Who are you?

00:16:53.180 --> 00:16:58.060
I am Waldlind Margrave Marrine Kreische's
lady-in-waiting, Layla.

00:16:58.060 --> 00:16:59.140
The same, Kamhi.

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:00.890
What do you want?

00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:05.150
Lord Milza, our mistress would like
to meet with you.

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:08.480
The Alliance leader, meet with me?

00:17:25.670 --> 00:17:28.920
I wonder what Alexis would think
if he hears about this battle...

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:31.590
My lady.

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:34.800
Enter.

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:38.810
So what did Crown Prince Milza say?

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:41.770
He said he'd like to meet
directly with you right away.

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:46.810
However, we were told to bring you alone.

00:17:50.650 --> 00:17:54.820
Unless we bring Dartania into the Alliance fold,
we can never defeat Altirk.

00:17:55.450 --> 00:17:56.990
Villar Constance...

00:17:58.320 --> 00:18:00.740
Turns out he did not have
what it takes to rule.

00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:05.210
I have no use for anyone who
lacks the will to unite the continent.

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:23.850
Announcing the Margrave of Waldlind,
Factory Alliance leader, Lady Marrine Kreische.

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:27.060
I am Milza Kuches, Crown Prince of Dartania.

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:31.610
I hear you seek my aid
in uniting the continent.

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:32.780
Yes.

00:18:32.780 --> 00:18:37.740
My father, Matthias, and I have inherited
the dream envisioned by my grandfather.

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:41.200
To unite the continent, and merge all Crests.

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:46.210
If the legend is true, the era of Chaos
will come to an end by doing so.

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:50.840
I have been told that you
desire to do the same.

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:52.960
Well, I'm not so sure.

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:58.090
I've been told how you met
and fell in love with Alexis Doucet.

00:18:58.090 --> 00:19:00.470
That's all in the past.

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:03.350
Let's not kid ourselves, shall we?

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:19.700
I don't care if it's only for tonight.

00:19:21.030 --> 00:19:22.740
I will make you my conquest.

00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:24.950
H-How vulgar!

00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:32.250
Even if you sleep with me,
you will have no claim over me.

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:33.460
I accept that.

00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:37.510
Think of it as a ritual for allies
about to go to war together.

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:40.640
Very well...

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:43.970
However, I have yet to be with a man.

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:48.020
I'll be leaving everything to you.
Is that acceptable?

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:46.080
I will not pledge loyalty to you.

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:49.830
But from this moment on,
I will become your sword.

00:20:50.210 --> 00:20:54.330
As long as you march down the path
of military rule, I swear to fight by your side.

00:22:01.030 --> 00:22:05.030
THE BLACK PRINCESS

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:40.040
EPISODE 10:
BLADE OF BETRAYAL
